@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final OrderRepository repository;

    public OrderService(OrderRepository repository) {
        this.repository = repository;
    }

    public void createBatch(List<Item> items) {
        for (Item item : items) {
            // Self-call: bypasses the proxy, so @Transactional does nothing here
            placeOrder(item);
        }
    }

    @Transactional
    public void placeOrder(Item item) {
        repository.save(new Order(item)); // NOT wrapped in a transaction
    }
}
```
*Because createBatch calls placeOrder on this, the call never goes through Spring's proxy, so no transaction starts.*

