@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final OrderProcessor processor; // separate bean = real proxy

    public OrderService(OrderProcessor processor) {
        this.processor = processor;
    }

    public void createBatch(List<Item> items) {
        // Calling another bean routes through its proxy, so each save is transactional
        items.forEach(processor::placeOrder);
    }
}

@Service
class OrderProcessor {
    private final OrderRepository repository;

    OrderProcessor(OrderRepository repository) {
        this.repository = repository;
    }

    @Transactional
    public void placeOrder(Item item) {
        repository.save(new Order(item)); // now wrapped in a transaction
    }
}
```
*Moving the transactional method to another bean means the call crosses a proxy boundary, so the transaction actually starts.*
